+        "description": "Currently Mintlify is hardcoded. Projects should choose their doc platform.\n\n## Current Hardcoding\n```bash\n# generate-changelog.sh line 10\nCHANGELOG_DST=\"$PROJECT_ROOT/docs/changelog/overview.mdx\"\n```\n\n## Proposed Config Schema\n```json\n{\n  \"release\": {\n    \"changelog\": {\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"format\": \"keep-a-changelog\",\n      \"autoGenerate\": true,\n      \"source\": \"CHANGELOG.md\",\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"platform\": \"mintlify\",\n          \"enabled\": true,\n          \"path\": \"docs/changelog/overview.mdx\",\n          \"template\": \"mintlify-changelog\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"platform\": \"docusaurus\",\n          \"enabled\": false,\n          \"path\": \"docs/changelog.md\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"platform\": \"github\",\n          \"enabled\": true,\n          \"useReleaseNotes\": true\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Supported Platforms\n1. **mintlify** - MDX with accordions (current)\n2. **docusaurus** - Standard markdown\n3. **github** - GitHub release notes\n4. **gitbook** - GitBook format\n5. **plain** - Keep-a-Changelog only (no conversion)\n6. **custom** - User-provided template\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Config schema supports multiple output platforms\n- [ ] Each platform can be enabled/disabled independently\n- [ ] Projects without Mintlify work correctly\n- [ ] Default preserves current behavior (Mintlify enabled)\n- [ ] `cleo init --detect` detects doc platform from existing files",
